      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://townofhomerny.gov/history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Homer Town Hall, built in 1908, celebrated its centennial in 2008 and began renovations to last another hundred years.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://townofhomerny.gov/history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Downtown Ghost Tour on Main St offers a spooky walk through murder mysteries and local apparitions.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://townofhomerny.gov/history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Glenwood Cemetery in East Homer holds graves of Civil War veterans, Lincoln’s painter, and the Cardiff Giant creator.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://townofhomerny.gov/history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Walking tours of East Homer’s historic sites last about an hour and a half, so wear comfortable shoes.",
